This study presents the results from SEM-TAB-FACTS, a novel sub-task under the NLP-TabData challenge that focused on analyzing and interpreting tables to verify factual claims and locate supporting evidence in scientific research papers. Participants were asked to engage in two key activities: first, to determine which rows in a table could be used to support a given claim; and second, to identify specific table cells that contained evidence to back up a given assertion. Evaluations using human annotated data showed that participants successfully completed both tasks to a satisfactory level. Specifically, the top performing system for the first task achieved 42.3 F1-score, while the top system for the second task reached an 81.5 F1-score. Notably, both systems demonstrated high levels of consistency, with a top system F1-score of 0.92 for task 1 and 0.93 for task 2. To facilitate further research, annotated data as well as code used in the task have been made publicly available for both tasks. Additionally, the technical papers and data have been uploaded to the SemEval 2021 website. The data can be accessed at: https://github.com/caglar/SEM-TAB-FACTS and https://www.semeval.org Tasks C and D. 

